// A **positional** variant payload (`Leaf(Widget)`) names a type, and that name is validated like
// every other annotation — an unresolvable one is E0013.
//
// It used to be *stored* unlike every other annotation: a positional payload parsed with its type
// in the field's *name* and no annotation at all, so the declaration walk's "check the annotation"
// step saw nothing, and this was the one type position in the language nobody validated — the named
// form `Leaf(item: Widget)` was correctly rejected while this one checked clean. The type lives in
// the type slot now, so the ordinary rule reaches it; this case pins that it still does.
// expect: error E0013 at 12:10
// expect: exit 1
enum Tree {
    Leaf(Widget);
    Nil;
}

echo 1;
